{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"nan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A NaN compares not equal, not greater than, and not less than every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value, including itself. Passing a NaN to an operation generally results"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in NaN."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let x = 1.21","\/\/ x > Double.nan == false","\/\/ x < Double.nan == false","\/\/ x == Double.nan == false"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because a NaN always compares not equal to itself, to test whether a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floating-point value is NaN, use its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isNaN"},{"type":"text","text":" property instead of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equal-to operator ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":"). In the following example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"y"},{"type":"text","text":" is NaN."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let y = x + Double.nan","print(y == Double.nan)","\/\/ Prints \"false\"","print(y.isNaN)","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/floatingpoint\/nan"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/F